      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. That is about 5 times the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (2,000\u20132,550 mg/day for most formulations). A single 4,250 mg dose is also more than the maximum daily dose. At this level there is a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **425 mg PO three times daily** (if the extra digit was a typo)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily** or another titration dose\n\nIf you do want 4250 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a brief clinical rationale. I'll then enter it with a note on the order. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
